  <div id="sutta">
  
    <h4 id="thag1.23" class="h1">Thag 1:23  Gosāla</h4>
            <div class="verse">
              <p>I—having eaten honey-rice</p>
              <p>in a bamboo patch</p>
              <p>and rightly grasping the aggregates’<span class="fn"><a href="#thag1.23note01">1</a></span><!--end fn cite--></p>
              <p>arising-disbanding—</p>
              <p class="v1">will return to the hillside, intent</p>
              <p class="v1">on seclusion.</p>
            </div><!--end verse-->
            <div class="note">
              <p class="notetitle">Note</p><!--end notetitle-->
              <p id="thag1.23note01">1. The aggregates of form, feeling, perception, fabrication, and consciousness. See <a href="../../SN/SN22_48.html">SN 22:48</a>, <a href="../../SN/SN22_59.html">SN 22:59</a>, and <a href="../../SN/SN22_79.html">SN 22:79</a>.</p>
            </div><!--end notes-->
      </div><!--end:sutta-->
    </div><!--end:content-->
    
